% of those age 65 or over. Coleman, Kenneth. A History of Georgia. Athens, GA: University of Georgia P, 1991. Harden, William. A History of Savannah and South Georgia. Vol. I. Chicago and New York: The Lewis Company, 1913. Joslyn, Mauriel P. Immortal\"}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0210-ad93362655ef:d01\", \"text\": \"males. The median income for a household in the county was $29,312, and the median income for a family was $34,753. Males had a median income of $30,228 versus $20,154 for females. The per capita income for the county was $13,894. About 15.50% of families and 20.10% of the population were below the poverty line, including 22.40% of those under age 18 and 25.50% of those age 65 or over. As of the 2010 United States Census, there were 14,593 people, 5,596 households, and 3,854 families residing in the county. The population density was . There were 6,739 housing units\"}], \"fallible_prior\": [], \"prior_explanation\": \"I do not have specific data on the median income for a family in Screven. This information would require access to recent economic or census data.\", \"fallible_cards\": [{\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0210-ad93362655ef:d00\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0210-ad93362655ef:d00:c0\", \"entity\": \"median income for a family in Screven\", \"scope\": \"city\", \"claim\": \"The median income for a family in the city was $31,250.\", \"answer\": \"$31,250\", \"quote\": \"household in the city was $25,714, and the median income for a family was $31,250.\", \"original_document_number\": 1}, {\"doc_id\": \"ramdocs-0210-ad93362655ef:d01\", \"card_id\": \"ramdocs-0210-ad93362655ef:d01:c0\", \"entity\": \"median income for a family in Screven\", \"scope\": \"county\", \"claim\": \"The median income for a family in the county was $34,753.\", \"answer\": \"$34,753\", \"quote\": \"The median income for a household in the county was $29,312, and the median income for a family was $34,753.\", \"original_document_number\": 2}]}"
